Hoist the 48 identical `T7·p0` products into one per-solve computation, and add profile regions.
Fused the unrolled 600-dim updates (112 → 81 µs). Next I'll try fusing the per-layer 20- and 30-row updates, since that's the remaining hot spot.
I sped the solver up from 112.3 µs to 60.0 µs per solve (about 1.87×), and `make verify` still prints `VERIFY OK` (worst error 3.1e-15). I only changed `src/fom_solver.c`; `src/fom_linsolve.c` has no linear solves in this unrolled problem, so it is untouched.

FOMTOOLS-SUMMARY-BEGIN
**Whole-solve time (`make bench`):** 112.27 µs at the start, 60.01 µs at the end, a **1.87× speedup**. `make verify` passes (worst max-abs error 3.1e-15; tolerance 1e-6).

**Final profile (`make profile`, mean 60.04 µs):**

| Region | Total over 5000 solves | Share |
|---|---|---|
| unrolled_layers | 238.6 ms | 79.6% |
| first_layers | 53.8 ms | 18.0% |
| state_update | 7.1 ms | 2.4% |
| param_hoist | 0.14 ms | 0.05% |

**Optimizations applied:**
1. **Compute the parameter term once per solve (112.3 → 112.0 µs).** `T7_P_P0 · p0` is the same in all 48 unrolled 30-dim layers, because `p0` doesn't change during a solve. It is now computed once into a 30-element stack buffer and copied into each layer, replacing 48 zero-fills plus CSR products.
2. **One-pass update for the 600-dim layers (→ 81.6 µs).** Valid because of structure in the matrices:
   - `T5_T_T2` is diagonal.
   - `T2_T_T1` and `T5_T_T4` have exactly one nonzero per row.
   
   So each of the 48 updates (copy the constant, three CSR products, box clip) becomes a single loop over 600 elements with no row-pointer loops. The additions happen in the original order.
3. **One-pass updates for the per-layer 20-dim (relu) and 30-dim layers (→ 60.0 µs).** Every one of the 98–99 per-layer operators has the same sparsity pattern; only the values differ:
   - The 20×600 operators have 30 contiguous nonzeros per row (columns 30i to 30i+29).
   - The 30×600 operators have 20 nonzeros per row at stride 30 (columns j+30k).
   - `T3_T_T1` and `T7_T_T4` have one nonzero per row.
   
   Each layer's update (constant, three CSR products, and relu for the 20-dim layers) became one fixed-shape loop with no column-index lookups. The values are copied as static data into `fom_solver.c`. The generator checked each pattern before using it, and the additions keep their original order.

The `FOM_PROF_BEGIN/END` markers stay in place around param_hoist, first_layers, unrolled_layers and state_update. There is still no dynamic allocation and no division.

**What's left:** the first layers use the 600×650 and 600×600 CSR operators in the fixed `fom_ops.c`, which can't be edited. The unrolled layers are now limited mainly by reading about 1 MB of per-layer coefficients on every solve.
FOMTOOLS-SUMMARY-END
